L000497	with $x = 1 - (K-1)/N$:
L000498	\[
L000499	    \ln \left( \binom{N}{K} \frac{K!}{N^K} \right) \leq N [ -1 + x(1 - \ln ( x )) ]; \forall K\geq 2.
L000500	\]
L000501	Now set $N$ to be large enough to have $x \approx 1 - \frac{K}{N}$ and $\frac{\delta}{\sqrt{N}} \ll 1$.
L000502	Our assumption that $K\geq \delta\sqrt{N}$ gives $x \leq 1 - \frac{\delta}{\sqrt{N}}$. If we now observe that $x(1-\ln(x))$ is increasing
L000503	for $x \leq 1$
L000504	\begin{align*}
