L000581	Inserting this expression of  $P_N(z)= \sum_{k=0}^N c_k \binom{N}{k}^{1/2} z^k$ in
L000582	the integral $I(N,R)$ and calculating the integral in polar coordinates  $z=re^{i\theta}$ we obtain
L000583	\[
L000584	I(N,R) = \sum_{k=0}^{N} \abs{c_k}^2 \binom{N}{k}\frac{2}{N^k} \int_{0}^{R}
L000585	r^{2k+1} e^{-r^2} dr.
